ng or impossible filing date are dropped and counted. Entering on the trade date is not achievable for the public."},{"id":"missing_tickers","text":"Rows without a usable ticker (bonds, funds without symbols, private assets, options) are excluded and counted. Ticker renames and reuse can cause mismatches."},{"id":"no_wrongdoing","text":"A statistical pattern in disclosed trades does not show use of nonpublic information."},{"id":"owner_unknown","text":"The data does not show whether a trade was the member's, a spouse's or a dependent's."},{"id":"price_basis","text":"Prices use adjusted close when available, otherwise close (price return only, no dividends)."},{"id":"short_history","text":"About five years of data and one market regime. There are few independent windows at 180 days."},{"id":"survivorship","text":"The price universe is the tickers Congress traded plus a fixed ETF set. Delisted or acquired names may be missing or cut short, which flatters stock-picking results."},{"id":"universe_bias","text":"Congress trades large, popular US names. Doing better than SPY can reflect that tilt, so results are also compared with random picks from the same universe."}]}
